Phase 7 item 3 (CDP bridge + Chromium launch) — E2E proof
Date: 2026-09-11

Scope proven (REAL headless Chromium, real WebSocket CDP transport):
1. Launch: MODBIT_BROWSER_BIN / per-OS discovery; --headless=new
   --remote-debugging-port=0 + throwaway profile (uniqueness defect fixed
   en route: colliding --user-data-dir makes Chrome delegate to a running
   singleton — suffix now full-nanos + per-process sequence);
   DevToolsActivePort handshake; browser-level WS attach via
   Target.getTargets/attachToTarget(flatten) — one socket, flattened
   session; Runtime/Page/Network domains scoped to the session.
2. navigate: Page.navigate + readyState settle loop.
3. snapshot: agent-native semantic state — PageState/SemanticElement
   (existing canonical machinery) built from live DOM (interactive
   elements with stable refs; url/title verified against the fixture).
4. action: Runtime.evaluate (click via JS) executed in the page.
5. console: Runtime.consoleAPICalled events buffered + drained (click log
   AND async fetch result, via pump() — events arriving between commands
   are filed, not lost).
6. network: Network.requestWillBeSent/responseReceived buffered +
   drained (GET /api + 200 observed).
7. capture: Page.captureScreenshot → real PNG (magic bytes + size).
8. Hostile-page test: prompt-injection text ("IGNORE ALL PREVIOUS
   INSTRUCTIONS...") passes through as verbatim page DATA (transport
   never parses/executes it); the page-authored exfil fetch to an
   attacker host is OBSERVED but never ANSWERED — no response line, the
   failed attempt surfaces as console data; only the local fixture
   server responds.
9. CI per-OS: find_browser() skips with a recorded note when no
   Chromium-family binary exists (documented gap, never a fake pass).

Reuse per work order: fingerprint/lease code untouched (PageState
fingerprints, ControllerLease, Watchdog in crates/browser); the CDP
module only moves bytes to and from the browser. Live-view/takeover UI
is desktop-side follow-up.

Post-condition proof added (M7.2/7.3/7.4): the fixture click now ALSO
mutates the DOM (appends an "Added" button); the post-action snapshot
moves the state FINGERPRINT, names the added element in the DELTA
(added=[button...Added], removed=[]), and the semantic snapshot carries
stable element refs throughout — semantic entities, fingerprint+delta,
and actions-with-observable-postconditions all driven through the real
CDP transport.

Test evidence: cargo test -p modbit-browser (12 unit + cdp_e2e:
cdp_bridge_drives_a_real_chromium_end_to_end,
hostile_page_content_stays_inert_data — green under full-workspace
parallel load, 544 tests total, 0 failed).
